<title>USA: Gaylord Communications names new president.</title>
<headline>Gaylord Communications names new president.</headline>
<dateline>NASHVILLE, Tenn. 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gaylord Entertainment Co said David Hall, 47, had been named president of its Gaylord Communications Group unit, effective December 1.</p>
<p>Hall, who was senior vice president of the unit's cable networks, would replace Tom Griscom, 69, who is retiring, the company said. Griscom had been with the company for 45 years.</p>
<p>Hall became chief engineer for Gaylord in 1975 and in 1983 was named general manager of Gaylord Communication's TNN, or The Nashville Network.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
